{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 16, :comments ["<b>And also He allured you</b> — like הסירך, as in: ויסיתם אלהים ממנו." "<b>Straight</b> — like: straight and narrow." "<b>Breadth</b> — to breadth that has no measure beneath it, for there is no measure in it, and it is by way of metaphor. For breadth is the surrounding circular line, and measure is the point." "<b>And the setting of your table</b> — and that which you set on your table, and this the Place [did] for you."], :book :job, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 36, :notes {0 "Ibn Ezra reads ואף הסיתך as equivalent to הסירך, apparently treating סית as an alternate/bet form of סור; the comparison verse is 2 Chronicles 32:15.", 1 "Ibn Ezra glosses צר with the phrase צר ומצוק, apparently reading the word as 'narrow/constricted' rather than 'enemy.'", 2 "מוצק here apparently refers to a geometric 'point' (the limiting dimension), though the term is unusual; translated hyper-literally.", 3 "המקום ('the Place') is a reverent epithet for God, rendered literally per the voice rule that divine names are not translated into English words."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Job -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/eyov/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:04:45.381300052Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}